{
  "title": "Increase SCALAR_LR from 0.5 to 0.7",
  "description": "Tuned per-layer residual path scales (resid_lambdas) by increasing SCALAR_LR from 0.5 to 0.7 to rebalance undertrained parameter group (120:1 imbalance with embeddings)",
  "status": "ok",
  "reflection": "Continued the successful parameter-group learning rate tuning strategy from Rounds 3-4. The per-layer residual scales (resid_lambdas) had extremely low effective LR (0.005 vs embeddings 0.6), creating a 120:1 imbalance similar to the unembedding:embedding ratio we fixed in Round 4. A 40% increase to 0.7 achieved val_bpb 0.993742, improvement of 0.001259 vs baseline 0.995001. This is the largest single improvement since Round 0 and confirms parameter-group LR tuning remains the high-ROI search direction. The gain suggests multiplicative layer parameters respond well to stronger gradients when other parameter groups are properly balanced."
}

